  "finalText": "I built the Crumb & Co sting as a 6 s, 1920×1080 comp on a warm paper background (`#F6EFE3`), using the hand-drawn organic style.\n\n- **Blobs:** three irregular blobs (**Blob sage**, **Blob terracotta**, **Blob mustard**) fade up from 0 to 1.3 s and then breathe slowly with a ±2% scale expression.\n- **Wheat:** **Wheat stalk** draws itself from the base up at 0.4 s over 1.4 s, with four pairs of grains and a tip.\n- **Loaf:** **Loaf outline** draws on at 1.4 s over 1.2 s, and **Loaf score** follows at 2.4 s with three slashes.\n- **Name:** **Name Crumb & Co** (serif, 150 px, ink) springs in at 3.0 s with a small rise and tilt.\n- **Underline:** **Mustard underline** scribbles under the name from 4.2 s.\n- **Boil:** the three line-art layers have a `wiggle(8, 0.5)` rotation expression, so the lines wobble slightly throughout.\n\nI checked eight frames across the piece. The sequence reads correctly and the final frame holds as a clean lockup. I didn't check the motion itself in playback, so the wobble and breathing speed are worth a look.\n\nPossible next tweaks: a bolder or more hand-lettered name, a sage leaf on the wheat, a different underline colour, or a looser, more jittery boil."
